within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.L_AntineoplasticAndImmunomodulatingAgents.L01E_ProteinKinaseInhibitors.L01EX02_Sorafenib;
model Sorafenib_Choi2021_PD_tumor_growth_inhibition
  "linear exposure-response sweep — Choi_2021 :: tumor-growth inhibition (tumor-growth inhibition)"
  extends Pharmacolibrary.Interfaces.PartialExposureResponseSweep(
    E0 = 0.0415,      // [cm3]
    Emax = 0, EC50 = 1,      // unused by a line
    exposure_per_s = 1);
  parameter Real slope = 0.0267   "[l/mg per day]";
equation
  response = E0 + slope*exposure;
  // family_inferred: the record's model family is transduction; read from the parameters: a slope and no Emax — linear
  annotation(experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 1000, Interval = 2),
    Documentation(info = "<html><body><h4>Sorafenib_Choi2021_PD_tumor_growth_inhibition</h4><p>The steady-state exposure-response curve of Choi YH et al., <i>The Journal of pharmacology and experimental therapeutics 377(3):305–315</i> 2021 (<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1124/jpet.121.000584\">doi:10.1124/jpet.121.000584</a>) — tumor-growth inhibition [cm3] against Sor milligram per liter — obtained by sweeping the driver instead of simulating a dose. Model family: linear.</p><h4>The parameters, in the paper's terms</h4><pre>  E0    =     0.0415 cm3      drug-free response (baseline) (w0 (initial tumor volume prior to administration), Q324)
  slope =     0.0267 l/mg per day change in response per unit of exposure (k2 (potency of the drug), Q335)</pre><p>The algebra is <code>response = E0 + slope*exposure</code>; this model only supplies the numbers. The x axis is one milligram per liter of Sor per second of simulated time: there is no state, no dose and no kinetics — plot <code>response</code> against <code>exposure</code> (or <code>time</code>).</p><h4>What it reproduces</h4><pre>  exposure = 0         response 0.0415   (drug-free)</pre></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Choi_2021: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: curated candidate</li></ul></body></html>"));
end Sorafenib_Choi2021_PD_tumor_growth_inhibition;
